#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:28
msgid "A machine-readable optical label that contains information about the item to which it is attached. In this context, it holds encrypted data that allows healthcare providers access to a pilgrim's IPS when scanned."
msgstr "Машиночитаемая оптическая метка, содержащая информацию о предмете, к которому она прикреплена. В данном контексте она содержит зашифрованные данные, которые при сканировании позволяют поставщикам медицинских услуг получить доступ к IPS паломника."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:22
msgid "A medical professional, such as a doctor or nurse, who provides clinical care to the pilgrim. Clinicians use the pilgrim's health information, accessed via the healthcare system, to offer appropriate medical treatments."
msgstr "Медицинский специалист, например врач или медсестра, оказывающий паломнику клиническую помощь. Клиницисты используют медицинскую информацию паломника, полученную через систему здравоохранения, для назначения надлежащего лечения."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:34
msgid "A security feature that adds an extra layer of protection to the pilgrim's health information. The default PIN is often the pilgrim's birthdate, and it is used in conjunction with the QR code to access the IPS."
msgstr "Функция безопасности, обеспечивающая дополнительный уровень защиты медицинской информации паломника. PIN по умолчанию часто является датой рождения паломника и используется вместе с QR-кодом для доступа к IPS."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:31
msgid "A Smart Health Link is a special link that provides time-bound, password and cryptographically restricted access to a health certificate or document."
msgstr "Smart Health Link — это специальная ссылка, обеспечивающая ограниченный по времени, защищённый паролем и криптографически ограниченный доступ к сертификату о состоянии здоровья или документу."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:43
msgid "An IPS document together with a digital signature that can be used to verify the provenance of the IPS within a Trust Network."
msgstr "Документ IPS вместе с цифровой подписью, которую можно использовать для проверки происхождения IPS в пределах Сети доверия."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:21
msgid "Clinician"
msgstr "Клиницист"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:36
msgid "EMR (Electronic Medical Record)"
msgstr "EMR (электронная медицинская запись)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:39
msgid "HIE (Health Information Exchange)"
msgstr "HIE (обмен медицинской информацией)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:12
msgid "Host Country"
msgstr "Принимающая страна"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:24
msgid "International Patient Summary (IPS)"
msgstr "Международная сводка о пациенте (IPS)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:1
msgid "Key concepts and abbreviations are described here. Additional terms are defined in the Glossary and List of Abbreviations in the <a0>WHO Digital Documentation of COVID-19 Certificates FHIR Implementation Guide</a0>."
msgstr "Здесь описаны ключевые концепции и сокращения. Дополнительные термины определены в глоссарии и списке сокращений в <a0>руководстве по внедрению FHIR ВОЗ «Цифровая документация сертификатов COVID-19» (WHO Digital Documentation of COVID-19 Certificates FHIR Implementation Guide)</a0>."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:4
msgid "Key Concepts and Definitions"
msgstr "Ключевые концепции и определения"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:9
msgid "Origin Country"
msgstr "Страна происхождения"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:6
msgid "Pilgrim"
msgstr "Паломник"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:33
msgid "PIN (Personal Identification Number)"
msgstr "PIN (персональный идентификационный номер)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:27
msgid "QR Code"
msgstr "QR-код"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:18
msgid "Registration Nurse"
msgstr "Регистрационная медсестра"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:30
msgid "Smart Health Link (SHL)"
msgstr "Smart Health Link (SHL)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:10
msgid "The country from which the pilgrim originates or holds citizenship. This is significant in the context of healthcare as health information and preparatory measures might be initiated in the origin country before the pilgrimage."
msgstr "Страна, из которой происходит паломник или гражданство которой он имеет. Это важно в контексте здравоохранения, поскольку сбор медицинской информации и подготовительные меры могут быть начаты в стране происхождения до паломничества."

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:42
msgid "Verifiable International Patient Summary (Verifiable IPS)"
msgstr "Проверяемая Международная сводка о пациенте (проверяемая IPS)"

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:25
msgid "A digital document that contains essential healthcare information about a patient, designed to support the continuity of care and patient safety. For pilgrims, the IPS includes basic demographics, medical history, medications, allergies, and other critical health information that can be shared across borders and healthcare systems."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:37
msgid "A digital version of a patient's paper chart, used by healthcare providers for diagnosis and treatment. In the context of the pilgrimage, EMRs are used by host country medical facilities to manage pilgrim care."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:19
msgid "A healthcare professional responsible for the initial registration of pilgrims at pilgrimage health facilities. This includes collecting and verifying pilgrim information and initiating the health service process."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:16
msgid "A medical facility set up to cater specifically to the needs of pilgrims. These facilities can range from clinics to hospitals and are equipped to handle both routine health checks and emergency services."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:7
msgid "A person who undertakes the pilgrimage. In the context of the healthcare system, the pilgrim is the primary user, receiving healthcare services and interacting with various healthcare providers."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:15
msgid "Pilgrimage Health Facility"
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:13
msgid "The country hosting the pilgrimage, which in this guide's examples is the fictional Taifafeki. The host country provides healthcare and other services to pilgrims during their stay."
msgstr ""

#: input/pagecontent/concepts.md:40
msgid "The electronic sharing of health information among different organizations. In the context of the pilgrimage, it refers to the system that allows origin countries and the host country to exchange pilgrim health information securely."
msgstr ""

